> Is there someway to get rid of a bone's file if it is too deadly?

In addition to what HJC said, and if you're really desperate, you can
also delete the bones file from your hard disk (as long as you play
on your machine or have sufficient privileges on the target system);
e.g. on my Linux box the Nethack directory is /usr/games/lib/nethackdir
and the files named something like bonXN.Z.gz (with appropriate values
for X, N, and Z). Just delete the respective file where the above 'X'
must be M (for mines), and Z matches the dungeon level in the branch.

